{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.StrongRankCondition","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasisCore","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtTriangularCore"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.specht_finrank_eq_numSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.specht_finrank_eq_numSYT","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasis.lean#L120-L140","doc":"**Standard-basis theorem (reduction).**\n`dim_k S^μ = #SYT(μ)`.\n\nProved sorry-free *from* `standardBasis` via `Module.finrank_eq_nat_card_basis`\n(which gives `finrank = Nat.card ι` directly, with no `Fintype` on the index),\nand `numSYT μ = Nat.card (StandardYoungTableau μ)` definitionally. Hence the only\nunproved inputs are the dominance core (now consumed by the proved triangular) and\n`standardPolytabloid_straightening` (spanning).\n\nCarries `[CharZero k]`, inherited from `standardBasis`. This declaration previously\nbore an `omit [CharZero k] in`, which made the file fail to compile: the proof\napplies `standardBasis`, which genuinely takes the instance, so the omitted binder\nleft `CharZero k` unsynthesizable at the application. The generality the `omit`\nasserted was never established — dropping it is what the existing proof supports.\n(The standard-polytabloid basis does exist over an arbitrary field, so the\nhypothesis is likely removable, but that needs the `CharZero` uses inside\n`standardBasis`'s own inputs traced and discharged — not an annotation change.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardBasis","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasis.lean#L104-L118","doc":"**The standard polytabloid basis** of `S^μ`, indexed by `StandardYoungTableau μ`.\n\nAssembled by `Basis.mk` from:\n* `standardPolytabloid_linearIndependent` (independence, via the proved triangular\n  core), and\n* `standardPolytabloid_span` (spanning, with the `≥ ⊤` direction supplied as\n  required by `Basis.mk`).\n\nThis definition is **sorry-free apart from the dominance core + the spanning stub**\n— all the `Basis.mk` plumbing (corestriction to `S^μ`, the `span ≥ ⊤` reshaping) is\ndischarged in the core file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasis.lean#L91-L100","doc":"**Content obligation 1/2 — linear independence**, now derived **sorry-free modulo\nthe single dominance core** via the proved `standardPolytabloid_triangular` (the\ntriangular lever + the corestriction reduction discharge everything else). Phrased on\nthe corestricted family `standardPolytabloidS` (valued in `S^μ`), as required by\n`Basis.mk`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_triangular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_triangular","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasis.lean#L77-L88","doc":"**The triangular family exists — PROVED.** There is a linear extension of\ndominance on `Tabloid μ` under which the standard polytabloids form a `Triangular`\nfamily with the concrete leading map `leadTab`. Historically the irreducible\ncombinatorial core of brick 4 (an honest `sorry` cited to Sagan Thm 2.5.2); now\n**proved sorry-free** by directly consuming the reassembled bundle\n`SpechtTriangularCore.standardPolytabloid_triangular'` (which discharges the two\norder-independent fields `diag_unit`, `lead_inj` fully and reduces `supp_le` to the\nrelation-level dominance lemma `SpechtDominanceCore.dominance_relation_exists`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}